how it works:
.feature file
   ↓
Cucumber
   ↓
Mapping Given / When / Then
   ↓
Step Definition (.ts)
   ↓
Playwright
   ↓
Browser
   ↓
Web Application


create first test case:
step 1: create a feature file
step 2: create a cucumber.json file for configuration under project folder 
step 3: edit package.json to convert default language JS to TS
step 4: run in VScode terminal $ npm test         //it looks at feature and step files
step 5: create a step file

example of cucumber.json:
{
    "default": {
        //make sure that one step starts after the previous one finishes (async function + await)
        //this setting is only for auto-generated snippets instead of existing steps
        "formatOptions": {
            "snippetInterface": "async-await"   
        },
        "paths": [
            "src/test/features/"
        ],
        //"publishQuiet": true,
        "dryRun": true              //check whether all the steps are defined and valid
        "require": [
            "src/test/steps/*.ts"
        ],
        "requireModule": [
            "ts-node/register"      //to solve the ts-import statement error
        ]
    }

an example of "async-await":
if feature file is as below:
Feature: Login
Scenario: Successful login
  Given I am on the login page
  When I enter my username
  Then I should see the homepage

and there's no step Definition of 'Given I am on the login page', when run $ npm test, cucumber would generate:
Given('I am on the login page', async function () {
  // Write code here
});

and we can add playwright into it:
Given('I am on the login page', async function () {
  await this.page.goto('/login');
});

which is this workflow:
Cucumber
   ↓
Generate async Step Definition
   ↓
we write Playwright
   ↓
await page.goto()
   ↓
Browser

note: currently a known issue of compatibility between ts-node and TypeScript 7 is that running $ npm test can fail with an error as below:
TypeError: Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'fileExists')
solution: downgrade TypeScript 7.0.2 to TS 6
$ npm install -D typescript@6.0.3
$ npm list typescript   //verify


hover on steps in the feature file, it shows 'cucumber.undefined-step' in tooltip, to solve it:
get into cucumber extension installation page again, it shows up paths of feature files under "cucumber.features" which is where we have to keep feature files,
and it shows paths of steps files under "cucumber.glue".
OR
settings -> settings -> search cucumber -> select Extensions: cucumber -> Edit in settings.json -> copy Related Path of feature folder and step folder -> add to 
"cucumber.features" and "cucumber.glue".
re-open feature file, hover again, a wavy underline shouldnt be showing anymore.

